      "block": "Basic_TextBlock",
      "purpose": "Explains false friends and why they matter after a lesson on cognates.",
      "data": {
        "eyebrow": "Unit 2.9",
        "title": "Not every look-alike is a friend",
        "sections": [
          {
            "paragraphs": [
              "Most look-alike words are real cognates: hotel is hotel. But a few are false friends: they look like an English word and mean something different. A handful of them can turn a simple sentence into a very awkward one.",
              "Learn these as a short warning list, each paired with the word you actually want."
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
